KSA ECC-Map — Licensing

This project mixes original content, code, and third-party data under different terms.

1. ORIGINAL MAPPING DATA & DOCUMENTATION
   The technique->control mappings (mappings/), the control-intent PARAPHRASES and
   structure we authored (catalog/*.json), and the documentation (docs/, README)
   are licensed under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0).
   https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

2. CODE
   The scripts (scripts/) are licensed under the MIT License.

3. THIRD-PARTY CONTENT — see NOTICE for full attribution:
   - NCA ECC-1:2018 and CSCC-1:2019 control IDs, numbering, and Arabic/English
     control TEXT are the property of the National Cybersecurity Authority (NCA),
     Kingdom of Saudi Arabia. They are REFERENCED here (IDs cited, intent
     paraphrased) and are NOT relicensed. The binding Arabic text governs.
   - The ATT&CK->NIST 800-53 corroboration data (corroboration/) is from MITRE
     Center for Threat-Informed Defense, under Apache License 2.0.
   - MITRE ATT&CK(R) technique IDs/names are used under the MITRE ATT&CK Terms of Use.

This project is community guidance and is NOT an NCA-endorsed compliance attestation.
